Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] Do not use noexcept for the forbidden C functions on Android

Bionic does not mark the C library functions as noexcept, so a declaration
with a noexcept exception specification does not match the declaration in
the system header and clang rejects the build with "missing exception
specification 'noexcept'".

---
--- a/src/hotspot/share/utilities/compilerWarnings.hpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/share/utilities/compilerWarnings.hpp
@@ -131,6 +131,14 @@
 #define FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_COND_NOEXCEPT_noexcept NOT_WINDOWS(NOT_BSD(noexcept))
 #define FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_COND_NOEXCEPT_
 
+// Android's bionic does not mark the C library functions as noexcept, so a
+// declaration with a noexcept exception specification does not match the
+// declaration in the system header and the build fails with "missing
+// exception specification 'noexcept'".
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#undef FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_COND_NOEXCEPT_noexcept
+#define FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_COND_NOEXCEPT_noexcept
+#endif
 
 #ifndef FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_IMPORT_SPEC
 #define FORBIDDEN_FUNCTION_IMPORT_SPEC
